  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "50148813",
      "title": "Understanding RAG & CAG",
      "sourceHash": "ae4d556b0244e10b25af909c95ba9a929575f18da2036721c208f39e4e964dfa",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.699,
          "end": 3.659,
          "en": "So what does RAG and CAG mean, and what",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.679,
          "end": 6.639,
          "en": "are these terms or concepts all about, and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.759,
          "end": 9.679,
          "en": "how can they help us? RAG stands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.719,
          "end": 12.539,
          "en": "for retrieval augmented generation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.599,
          "end": 14.739,
          "en": "and CAG stands for cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.939,
          "end": 17.46,
          "en": "augmented generation, and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.699,
          "end": 20.62,
          "en": "both concepts are about enhancing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.659,
          "end": 23.459,
          "en": "the prompt that we're sending to an AI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.559,
          "end": 25.84,
          "en": "model with extra",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.139,
          "end": 29.119,
          "en": "information, with extra data that's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.139,
          "end": 32.04,
          "en": "then taken into account by that model, so that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.059,
          "end": 34.819,
          "en": "the AI model then is able to generate an",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.899,
          "end": 37.72,
          "en": "answer that does not just relate to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.739,
          "end": 40.439,
          "en": "our prompt, but also to that extra",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.459,
          "end": 42.64,
          "en": "data we pulled into the prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.559,
          "end": 46.439,
          "en": "And that's what this augmented part in these names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.5,
          "end": 48.979,
          "en": "means. We augment, we enhance the prompt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.399,
          "end": 52.139,
          "en": "with extra data. Now, what's the difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.159,
          "end": 54.379,
          "en": "between retrieval and cache augmented?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.059,
          "end": 57.879,
          "en": "Retrieval augmented generation, RAG,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.219,
          "end": 61.079,
          "en": "is all about fetching data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.079,
          "end": 64.059,
          "en": "related to the question or prompt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.399,
          "end": 66.719,
          "en": "sent by the user. So if a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.259,
          "end": 70.119,
          "en": "asks about data about a certain employee, for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.159,
          "end": 73.119,
          "en": "example, the employee John Smith, we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.179,
          "end": 75.719,
          "en": "try to fetch data we have about John",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.059,
          "end": 78.999,
          "en": "and add that into the prompt, inject that into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.019,
          "end": 81.739,
          "en": "the prompt. And this injection, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.759,
          "end": 84.679,
          "en": "typically happens invisible behind the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.719,
          "end": 87.519,
          "en": "scenes, and you'll see how to build such a workflow in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.57900000000001,
          "end": 89.399,
          "en": "this section. We'll do that together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.619,
          "end": 93.57900000000001,
          "en": "And then the AI model can generate a meaningful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.619,
          "end": 96.559,
          "en": "response, a meaningful text based on our prompt and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.57900000000001,
          "end": 99.479,
          "en": "that data we have about John Smith or whatever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.499,
          "end": 102.419,
          "en": "we're pulling into that prompt. So with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.419,
          "end": 105.15899999999999,
          "en": "retrieval augmented generation, we're trying to fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.219,
          "end": 107.959,
          "en": "relevant data and inject that into the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.979,
          "end": 110.739,
          "en": "prompt. With cache augmented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.759,
          "end": 113.13900000000001,
          "en": "generation, we instead fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.239,
          "end": 115.87899999999999,
          "en": "all possibly relevant data, so for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.899,
          "end": 118.259,
          "en": "example, not just the data about John",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.339,
          "end": 120.899,
          "en": "Smith, but instead the data about all our",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.999,
          "end": 123.959,
          "en": "employees, and we inject that into the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.999,
          "end": 126.859,
          "en": "prompt. And then we have the AI model",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.959,
          "end": 129.079,
          "en": "generate a meaningful response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.399,
          "end": 132.859,
          "en": "Now, the advantage of retrieval augmented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132.959,
          "end": 135.659,
          "en": "generation, since we only fetched the relevant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.719,
          "end": 138.399,
          "en": "data there, is that it's pretty efficient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.459,
          "end": 141.439,
          "en": "and secure. There is no danger of leaking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.539,
          "end": 144.139,
          "en": "data that's actually not related to the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.199,
          "end": 147.179,
          "en": "prompt sent by the user, but it requires more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.219,
          "end": 150.199,
          "en": "complex setup because we need to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.219,
          "end": 152.539,
          "en": "what the user's prompt is about, then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.839,
          "end": 155.679,
          "en": "fetch relevant data, and then inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.779,
          "end": 158.659,
          "en": "that into the prompt. And we may, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 158.719,
          "end": 161.679,
          "en": "miss loosely related data because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 161.75900000000001,
          "end": 164.47899999999998,
          "en": "our data retrieval mechanism or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 164.639,
          "end": 167.139,
          "en": "code may be written such that it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.599,
          "end": 170.539,
          "en": "just fetches the most likely related, uh,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.579,
          "end": 173.25900000000001,
          "en": "record and not all possibly related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.399,
          "end": 176.359,
          "en": "records. And therefore, we might occasionally, depending on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.379,
          "end": 179.219,
          "en": "the kind of question we're tackling, miss",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 179.41899999999998,
          "end": 182.299,
          "en": "some data here. Now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.359,
          "end": 185.059,
          "en": "when it comes to cache augmented generation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.479,
          "end": 188.439,
          "en": "we're definitely working with a less efficient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.75900000000001,
          "end": 191.559,
          "en": "workflow because we load all the data that could",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.599,
          "end": 194.579,
          "en": "possibly be relevant, and we therefore need a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 194.619,
          "end": 197.539,
          "en": "model with a large context window depending on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 197.579,
          "end": 200.359,
          "en": "the amount of data we're fetching. Because if we're fetching, like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 200.939,
          "end": 203.839,
          "en": "3,000 rows of employee data, we need a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.899,
          "end": 206.819,
          "en": "context window that actually allows us to inject all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.859,
          "end": 209.579,
          "en": "that data into it along with the original",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.679,
          "end": 212.47899999999998,
          "en": "user prompt. But the advantage of cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 212.519,
          "end": 215.239,
          "en": "augmented generation, of course, is that it's less",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 215.31900000000002,
          "end": 218.279,
          "en": "complex because we don't need any complex data fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 218.31900000000002,
          "end": 221.119,
          "en": "mechanism. We just get all the data, and that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.079,
          "end": 224.639,
          "en": "And it can, of course, also help in situations where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 225.139,
          "end": 228.039,
          "en": "we might have loosely related data that might be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 228.159,
          "end": 230.939,
          "en": "missed by a more specific data fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 230.959,
          "end": 233.75900000000001,
          "en": "mechanism. And that's why we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233.81900000000002,
          "end": 236.519,
          "en": "these two main approaches. And in the end, it comes down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.539,
          "end": 239.359,
          "en": "to your specific use case, how",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 239.399,
          "end": 242.079,
          "en": "complex of a solution you want, and the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.139,
          "end": 244.939,
          "en": "AI model and its context window you're working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 244.959,
          "end": 247.919,
          "en": "with. In this section here, I'll show you both",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 247.919,
          "end": 250.719,
          "en": "approaches, and I'll give you examples for both",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 250.739,
          "end": 251.47899999999998,
          "en": "approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ],
      "lectureOrder": 277,
      "videoOrder": 277
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
